WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.660 --> 00:00:04.740
The ever-changing cast of "House of&nbsp;
the Dragon" can be hard to pin down,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.540
so here's a handy guide to all the new&nbsp;
Targaryen offspring — blonde and otherwise.

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:13.560
Thanks to a ten year time jump in the sixth&nbsp;
episode, entitled "The Princess and the Queen,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:18.469
a big chunk of the cast is now all grown&nbsp;
up, and they've all got kids of their own.

00:00:18.469 --> 00:00:22.789
"Ugh. You are nearly a man grown, how&nbsp;
is it that you can be so short-sighted?"

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:26.880
Considering that "House of the Dragon" has&nbsp;
already been renewed for a second season and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:31.500
promises to bring viewers through the entirety of&nbsp;
the Targaryen civil war known as the Dance of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:37.560
Dragons, these kids will, with absolute certainty,&nbsp;
play enormous roles in the infighting to come.

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:43.740
That said, it can be tough to parse which children&nbsp;
belong to whom or how and why they might even be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:48.960
important. So who are the Targaryen offspring that&nbsp;
we need to know about, and why do they matter?

00:00:49.511 --> 00:00:51.611
"This is the stuff, Lyonel!"

00:00:51.611 --> 00:00:56.100
As the sixth episode kicks off, Rhaenyra is&nbsp;
deep in the throes of childbirth with her third&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:01.560
son — whom her husband surprise-christens&nbsp;
"Joffrey", after his dead lover — but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:07.440
the ones who really matter right now are&nbsp;
Jacaerys and Lucarys, aka Jace and Luke.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:11.280
Introduced when they meet their baby&nbsp;
brother, there's one thing instantly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.420
noticeable about these two boys:&nbsp;
they don't have platinum blonde hair,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:19.860
while their parents, born of Houses&nbsp;
Targaryen and Velaryon, definitely do.

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:24.360
Anyone who remembers Ned Stark muttering&nbsp;
"Baratheon, black of hair" in the first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:28.800
season of "Game of Thrones" probably knows&nbsp;
where this storyline is going. Turns out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.060
considering Laenor, well, doesn't bat&nbsp;
for Rhaenyra's team, she outsourced her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:38.421
childbearing years to Ser Harwin Strong, Captain&nbsp;
of the City Watch and a confirmed brunette.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:44.728
"Do keep trying, Ser Laenor. Sooner or&nbsp;
later, you may get one who looks like you."

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:50.280
All that said, Rhaenyra's children are definitely&nbsp;
Targaryens. In the episode, Jacaerys works on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:55.140
training his dragon, Vermax, who's quite young&nbsp;
but is already responding well to his commands.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.140 --> 00:02:00.300
Lucarys is still quite young, but it's mentioned&nbsp;
that his traditional Targaryen dragon egg hatched&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:05.460
in his crib as well, so it stands to reason that&nbsp;
both brothers will be on dragonback soon enough.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:10.560
Far away from their cousins in King's&nbsp;
Landing, Baela and Rhaena — who seem to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.040
be named for their Targaryen ancestor&nbsp;
Baelon as well as Laena's mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:18.960
Rhaenys — are stranded with their parents&nbsp;
Laena Velaryon and Prince Daemon Targaryen.

00:02:18.960 --> 00:02:22.680
Though they lead a seemingly peaceful&nbsp;
and bountiful life out in Pentos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:25.920
the girls dream of more. In one&nbsp;
scene in "The Princess and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:30.420
Queen," Rhaena laments not having a dragon&nbsp;
egg from birth as her sister Baela does,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.420 --> 00:02:34.260
while Laena reassures her that&nbsp;
she'll go on to be a rider someday.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.880
However, these two young girls are struck&nbsp;
by tragedy when their mother Laena, in labor&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:42.720
with their younger brother, encounters&nbsp;
complications that can't be overcome.

00:02:43.225 --> 00:02:45.385
"I've reached the limit of my art."

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:52.200
Laena opts to burn herself and the burgeoning&nbsp;
baby alive with the help of her dragon Vhagar,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:56.700
leaving her daughters alone with their father&nbsp;
Daemon. These two girls may be motherless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.700 --> 00:03:01.020
but they have Velaryon and Targaryen blood&nbsp;
in their veins, unlike Rhaenyra's children.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:07.140
The blondest children on the show thus far,&nbsp;
Aegon II, Aemond, and Helaena are the issue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.640
of Alicent and her much-older husband,&nbsp;
Rhaenyra's father King Viserys. Blessed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:16.800
with the icy hair of the Targaryen family, their&nbsp;
parentage doesn't stand in doubt for a second,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:20.820
and upon Aegon's birth, there's a bit of&nbsp;
a kerfuffle over the line of succession.

00:03:20.820 --> 00:03:24.780
Despite previously naming Rhaenyra&nbsp;
as his official heir, Aegon's mere&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:30.060
existence places King Viserys in a bind. The&nbsp;
Seven Kingdoms may not accept a female ruler,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:36.000
and with a male heir at long last, it might make&nbsp;
more sense to put Aegon on the throne. Viserys&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:40.860
sticks by his daughter, but as he ages,&nbsp;
it's clear that his wife has other plans.

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:45.960
"The Princess and the Queen" is the first&nbsp;
glimpse we get of Aegon as an older child, and,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:49.980
honestly? He's kind of a jerk. He&nbsp;
bullies his younger brother Aemond&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:54.000
by giving him a pig instead of a dragon&nbsp;
and fights dirty during his training,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:58.320
showing himself to be pretty&nbsp;
smug and largely insufferable.

00:03:58.320 --> 00:04:02.340
By contrast, Aemond and Helaena have&nbsp;
shown themselves to be much quieter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.320
Helaena seems to like playing with centipedes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.880
while poor Aemond just wants to follow&nbsp;
in his family's massive footsteps.

